  "description": "FIWHAX crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C94 H104 Cl2 Dy6 N6 O22 2+,3(C2 H6 O1),C2 H3 N1,2(Cl1 1-). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.490-3.888 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 91.76-111.61°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C102H125Cl4Dy6N7O25. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
